 "standard_text": "Use a range of techniques to perform and check written and mental calculations of whole numbers, including estimation, building up and breaking down numbers, rounding off and compensating, doubling and halving, using a number line, and using addition and subtraction as well as multiplication and division as inverse operations.",
 "meta_desc": "Free CAPS Grade 4 mental maths worksheets on calculation techniques: estimation, rounding off and compensating, doubling and halving, breaking down numbers and inverse operations. 100 questions with memos.",
 "key_big": "Round off, calculate, then compensate.",
 "key_sub": "Check with the inverse operation.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How to think about it</h2><ul><li><b>Estimate</b> by rounding off first: 3 897 + 2 104 is about 4 000 + 2 000 = 6 000.</li><li><b>Compensate</b>: 2 456 + 198 = 2 456 + 200 − 2 = 2 654.</li><li><b>Double and halve</b>: 25 × 48 = 50 × 24 = 1 200.</li><li><b>Break down</b> numbers: 347 + 225 = 300 + 200 + 40 + 20 + 7 + 5.</li><li>Addition and subtraction are <b>inverse operations</b>; so are multiplication and division.</li></ul><h2>Examples</h2><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>5 342 − 299</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>5 342 − 300 = 5 042</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>add back 1</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: 5 043</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><div class='sn-tw'><table class='sn-table'><thead><tr><th>Mistake</th><th>What to do instead</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Compensating the wrong way</td><td>You took away 1 too many, so add 1 back.</td></tr><tr><td>Doubling only part</td><td>Double every part of the number.</td></tr><tr><td>Same operation to undo</td><td>Undo + with −, × with ÷.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "What does CAPS Grade 4 say about calculation techniques?",
